<exercise>
    <statement>
        <p>
            Show that the function <md>
                f(x) = \frac{x^2 + 3x + 4}{x^2 - 1}
            </md>
            is not continuous at <m>x = \pm 1</m>. Is it possible to redefine <m>f</m> at these points to make the function continuous? If so, what should those values be?
        </p>
    </statement>
    <solution component="a">
        <p>
            
        </p>
    </solution>
</exercise>

<exercise>
